# Copy to .env.local if needed
# Zero-retention architecture: no server-side storage.
# Add API keys here when integrating OCR, LLM, or other services:
#
# Ask / Q&A (`/api/ask`) — Together AI (OpenAI-compatible). See Ask-integration-plan.md.
# TOGETHER_API_KEY=
# Default model: meta-llama/Meta-Llama-3-8B-Instruct-Lite (Meta Llama 3 8B, serverless on Together).
# Override examples: meta-llama/Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct-Turbo, or your dedicated Llama 3.1 8B endpoint name.
# For dedicated Llama 3.1 8B: set TOGETHER_MODEL to the endpoint’s name; set TOGETHER_BASE_URL only if Together shows a custom host.
# TOGETHER_MODEL=
# TOGETHER_BASE_URL=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# DEEPL_API_KEY=
# DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=
#
# Summary (`/api/summarize`) — Hugging Face Inference Providers router (OpenAI-compatible).
# Required for Summary on translate page; unrelated to Ask/Together.
# Use a fine-grained token with “Make calls to Inference Providers” (or classic token with inference scope).
# HF_TOKEN=
# Optional override if the default model is unavailable on your account or region:
# HF_SUMMARIZE_MODEL=meta-llama/Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct:cheapest
#
# --- Observability (Winnie / Team 1 eval ticket) — optional placeholders ---
# When wired, LangSmith (or LangChain tracing) can ingest `/api/ask` runs alongside the
# structured console logs (`[ask] request received`, etc.). Keys are never logged in plaintext.
# LANGSMITH_API_KEY=
# LANGSMITH_TRACING=true
# LANGSMITH_PROJECT=multilingual-doc-assistant
# Legacy LangChain env names also work if your org uses them:
# LANGCHAIN_API_KEY=
# LANGCHAIN_TRACING_V2=true
# LANGCHAIN_PROJECT=multilingual-doc-assistant
# REPLICATE_API_TOKEN=
# XTTS_REPLICATE_MODEL=lucataco/xtts-v2
# XTTS_SPEAKER_WAV_URL=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lucataco/cog-xtts-v2/main/female.wav
# MINIMAX_REPLICATE_MODEL=minimax/speech-02-turbo
# MINIMAX_FEMININE_VOICE_ID=Wise_Woman
# MINIMAX_MASCULINE_VOICE_ID=Deep_Voice_Man
# MINIMAX_AUDIO_FORMAT=mp3
#
# Local Coqui TTS sidecar (English, Spanish, Vietnamese). Start with: cd services/coqui-tts && source .venv/bin/activate && python server.py
# COQUI_TTS_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5002
# COQUI_TTS_FEMININE_SPEAKER=p228
# COQUI_TTS_MASCULINE_SPEAKER=p226
# Optional: override pretrained model names on the Python side (export before starting server.py)
# COQUI_TTS_EN_MODEL=tts_models/en/vctk/vits
# COQUI_TTS_ES_MODEL=tts_models/es/css10/vits
# COQUI_TTS_VI_MODEL=tts_models/vie/fairseq/vits
